@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Plan — rotate the GitHub tokens when one is rate limited
+
+## 1. Tests
+
+- [ ] 1.1 The retryer moves to the next token when the current one is rate limited (tests/retryer.test.js::`Test Retryer > retryer should return value and have 2 retries`) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.2 The retryer gives up after the eighth token (tests/retryer.test.js::`Test Retryer > retryer should throw error if maximum retries reached`) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.3 fetchStats shows GitHub's error message (tests/fetchStats.test.js::`Test fetchStats > should throw error`) [AC-2]
+- [ ] 1.4 fetchRepo goes through the token rotation (tests/fetchRepo.test.js::`Test fetchRepo > should fetch the repo through the token rotation`) [AC-3]
+
+## 2. The retryer
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Add the retryer over PAT_1 to PAT_8 (src/retryer.js)
+- [ ] 2.2 Let `request` take its headers from the caller (src/utils.js)
+- [ ] 2.3 Send the stats and repo queries through the retryer (src/fetchStats.js, src/fetchRepo.js)
+- [ ] 2.4 Cache both cards for 30 minutes (api/index.js, api/pin.js)
